          <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, but natural and organic formulation requires careful attention to stability, preservation and compatibility. Plant-derived ingredients can oxidise, vary between harvests and interact with other components. Establish the intended certification standard early, as this affects ingredient selection, formulation and labelling.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What is scale-up in serum manufacturing?<span class="plus"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-a"><p>Scale-up is the process of transferring a laboratory serum formula to commercial production. Batch size, mixing equipment, heating and cooling rates and addition order can all change the finished product. Pilot batches help identify issues before full production. Documentation of process parameters ensures consistency.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How do I choose a serum formulation consultant?<span class="plus"></span></button>
          <div class="faq-a"><p>Look for formal cosmetic science training, practical formulation experience, a whole-product view that includes packaging and manufacturing, plain-language communication, and honesty about trade-offs and limitations. Be cautious of anyone promising guaranteed results or a perfect formula on the first try.</p></div>
